  "reading": "All 66 sides lie between +0.011 and +0.067 (log). If net moments share D_x, the GT24 lever bias is 0.962, 3.2 % below the GT23 calibration (0.9942); 56/66 sides fall inside the pre-registered band around the GT23 centre and the 10 outside are all on the high side (0.055-0.067). If net moments were divided by body mass, the ratios would sit near log(body/worn) - log(b), about -0.06 to -0.12 for a bias near GT23; none does. Body mass is excluded unless the GT24 bias were about 0.86-0.91. The bias transfers only approximately (about 3 %), so E3 supports D_net = D_x within a few percent, not exactly."
